21. Best Time to Buy and Sell Stock ⭐
Easy–Medium
Pattern: Greedy · One-pass array traversal
Given an array of stock prices, find the maximum profit you can make by buying once and selling later.
Example: prices = [7, 1, 5, 3, 6, 4]
Output: 5
Explanation: Buy at 1, sell at 6. Profit = 6 - 1 = 5.


Solution:

const nums = [7, 1, 5, 3, 6, 4];
let min = nums[0];
let maxProfit = 0;

for (let i = 0; i < nums.length; i++) {
  let currentPrice = nums[i];
  let profit = currentPrice - min;

  if (currentPrice < min) {
    min = currentPrice;
  }

  if (profit > maxProfit) {
    maxProfit = profit;
  }
}

console.log(maxProfit);
